  "usage_note": "**A bit** before an adjective is very common in speech and means *slightly*: *a bit cold*. It is especially common with words for something unwelcome (*a bit tired*, *a bit late*), where it makes a complaint sound softer. Before a noun, use **a bit of**: *a bit of bread*.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "Can I have a bit bread?",
      "correct": "Can I have a bit of bread?",
      "note": "Before a noun you need **of**: *a bit of bread*, *a bit of help*."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "I'm a bit of tired.",
      "correct": "I'm a bit tired.",
      "note": "Before an adjective, use **a bit** with no **of**."
    }
  ],
